# C++ Simulation Core

Details: `docs/engineering/cpp.md`. Contract: TZ §5–9.

`src/sim` is the only world. It builds and tests with **no Godot headers**. Clients send intents, never desired state.

```cpp
// BAD
void SetGold(World&, int);
#include <godot_cpp/godot.hpp>

// GOOD
std::expected<TradeResult, TradeError> execute_trade(World&, const OfferTrade&);
```

Do: RAII; `std::expected` for ordinary failure; seeded RNG as world state; integer ticks/money; `unordered_map` lookup-only; concrete types until a second implementation exists.

Don't: god-object `World` + service locator; ECS/job system on day one; `nlohmann::json` as domain; `shared_ptr` everywhere; exceptions as “not enough gold”; `std::random_device` / wall clock as gameplay.
